      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a valid concern that the focus on political messaging in contemporary art could overshadow other aspects of artistic discipline and aesthetic quality. This doesn't necessarily equate to a decline in quality universally, as the art world encompasses a broad spectrum of value systems. Artistic worth can be multifaceted, as some art critics and audiences may still place high regard on technical skill and visual experience, while others may perceive the impactful thinking and societal engagement as equally, if not more, important. The idea of \"objective worth\" itself can be quite subjective and varies greatly across cultures, historical periods, and personal tastes. Deconstruction challenges fixed notions and opens up art to diverse interpretations, including the significant value of thought-provoking content.",
